Z||000000||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||07-31-2000||10:58 PM||||<BR>How do I know if my car has had the recall?  What do I look for?  I have a leak that started a couple of days ago, and just keeps getting worse.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I prefer to mot have to buy new manifolds if Pontiac will pay for it.  If I did have the recall fixed, then what is a good maniflod to buy and price?  Thanks...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Heisenhund||08-01-2000||07:22 AM||||Hiya Jeff,<P>The last step of the recall is to place a sticker showing completion under the hood. The full extent of the recall can be seen at this address:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm</A> <P>Best of luck....from another owner of a 1986½ GT<P>Heis<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||wwh0001||08-01-2000||10:43 AM||||Until recently you could call 1-800-PMCARES , give them your VIN and they could tell you if the recall has been done, their records are purged and they can no longer do that. They will just say there are no outstanding recalls . FOr this recall the rubber stip on the hood should have been removed and a sticker place under the hood; but most dealors didn't do this, best way to tell is to check your front Manifold. If there is a piece of metal under the manifold that is attached at the ports and goes down the engine ( this is the heat shield) the recall has been done.||||reg||1
